<title>FINLAND: BUDGET CHIEF VIRTANEN SAYS FINLAND READY FOR EMU.</title>
<headline>BUDGET CHIEF VIRTANEN SAYS FINLAND READY FOR EMU.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finance ministry budget chief Erkki Virtanen said on Tuesday that Finland was in shape to join EMU and that Finland belonged among the hard core of nations about to implement the single currency in 1999.</p>
<p>&quot;The Finnish national economy is certainly in shape for EMU ... we can easily move into the EMU-world from the start of 1999,&quot; Virtanen told a seminar.</p>
<p>&quot;Finland belongs in the hard core of EMU which will create the third stage of EMU from the beginning of 1999,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>--Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, news@reuters.fi</p>
</text>
